% A repeated variable in an all_different scope: `all_different_int([x, y, x])` says x is
% different from itself, so it is unsatisfiable however wide the domains are.
%
% lib/flatzinc/compile.ml decomposes it rather than handing the repeat to [Alldiff],
% whose Hall-set membership test is by NAME and would see two snapshots of one variable.
% The pair (x, x) becomes `x - x <> 0` through the ordinary post_ne path -- the ground
% contradiction test/models/ne_self_unsat.fzn already documents -- and the rest of the
% scope still becomes a global. So the refutation here is int_ne's, not Hall's, and that
% is the point: the decomposition is where the degenerate shape is answered.
var 1..3: x :: output_var;
var 1..3: y :: output_var;
constraint all_different_int([x, y, x]);
solve satisfy;
